arly retain-marker check on `exc` observes it (the model-level tag alone is invisible to fallback_on(exc)).","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Make should_fall_back leg-aware: a NON-PRIMARY leg's failure is always retained (returns True)' and 'Each non-primary candidate is tagged in build_fallback_model via a small _wrap_fallback_leg WrapperModel.'","Scope: 'leg-aware should_fall_back (early retain-marker check + two-rule docstring), _FALLBACK_LEG_ATTR, _fallback_leg_wrapper_class, _tag_fallback_leg, _wrap_fallback_leg'","src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py:366 `def should_fall_back(exc: Exception) -> bool:` — the predicate receives ONLY the exception, no leg/model handle.","src/rebar/llm/tracing.py:235-243 — the existing WrapperModel precedent (_TracedCandidateModel.request) catches and re-raises WITHOUT stamping any attribute onto the exception, so the propagation mechanism cannot be inferred from precedent.","pydantic_ai.models.wrapper.WrapperModel and pydantic_ai.exceptions.FallbackExceptionGroup both resolve (tool-verified)."],"finding":"Change 1 makes should_fall_back 'leg-aware' by an 'early retain-marker check' of _FALLBACK_LEG_ATTR, but the marker is described as tagged on the fallback-leg WrapperModel while pydantic-ai's FallbackModel invokes fallback_on(exc) with the raised EXCEPTION only; the plan never specifies how _FALLBACK_LEG_ATTR reaches the exception the predicate inspects (i.e. that the leg wrapper's request() must catch and stamp the marker onto the raised exception before re-raising).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4ae9fc0c88eb0bd8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan — Change 1 (model_classes.py: leg-aware should_fall_back + _FALLBACK_LEG_ATTR / _wrap_fallback_leg); Scope bullet for src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py","norm_id":"nb0c3803aae42d212","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executo